WEBVTT

00:29.291 --> 00:30.958
Not enough.

00:35.208 --> 00:36.666
Not enough!

00:43.000 --> 00:45.208
Kokushu the Manslayer.

00:46.000 --> 00:47.958
I haven't had enough fun yet.

00:48.875 --> 00:50.166
Let's fight to the death.

00:53.208 --> 00:54.916
The battle is over.

00:58.208 --> 01:00.083
But we're samurai.

01:00.916 --> 01:02.250
We fight on regardless.

01:04.541 --> 01:06.666
It ends too quickly, huh?

01:07.375 --> 01:10.166
These sons of bitches
with their rifles and cannons.

01:14.708 --> 01:15.583
See?

01:16.500 --> 01:18.291
That's all it takes.

01:19.416 --> 01:21.208
It doesn't even feel like killing.

01:21.708 --> 01:23.750
What a civilized weapon.

01:27.166 --> 01:29.500
The age of the sword is coming to an end.

01:32.833 --> 01:35.041
Manslayers like us are no longer needed.

01:35.541 --> 01:38.125
That doesn't change who we are inside.

01:38.625 --> 01:41.166
We'll always be manslayers.

01:43.750 --> 01:47.333
I liked the way you killed back there.

01:49.166 --> 01:51.000
Come and show me how you do it.

02:26.083 --> 02:28.250
You feel like fighting me yet?

02:54.458 --> 02:56.000
Kill me.

03:02.791 --> 03:04.958
If you don't kill me now,

03:05.041 --> 03:07.791
I'll hunt you down
for the rest of my life.

03:12.041 --> 03:13.625
It's over now.

03:24.500 --> 03:27.000
We'll meet again, all right?!

03:28.291 --> 03:30.916
Kokushu the Manslayer!

03:52.083 --> 03:56.333
The era of the samurai is over.
You just stay here until the day you die.

04:23.000 --> 04:26.375
I wanna fight…

04:38.333 --> 04:42.208
What a sorry sight you make,
Bukotsu Kanjiya.

04:43.541 --> 04:46.000
You disappeared ten years ago,

04:46.500 --> 04:49.000
then suddenly reemerged
for the Satsuma Rebellion

04:49.500 --> 04:51.625
and even cut down your own allies.

04:55.083 --> 04:57.208
How have you lived your life since then?

05:01.625 --> 05:04.708
How have I lived my life?

05:07.541 --> 05:09.500
I've been dead

05:10.750 --> 05:12.541
this whole time.

05:15.625 --> 05:20.500
I'm going to give you another chance
to live as a samurai.

05:23.375 --> 05:24.583
Huh?

05:34.750 --> 05:36.333
HOKOKU NEWSPAPER
PARTICIPANTS WANTED

06:01.291 --> 06:02.958
Hey! What's going on?!

06:49.666 --> 06:53.000
LAST SAMURAI STANDING

06:57.583 --> 06:58.750
TO TOSHIYOSHI KAWAJI

06:58.833 --> 07:02.375
WE MUST DISCUSS THE FUTURE OF THE POLICE.
I AWAIT YOU IN TOKYO.

07:05.958 --> 07:07.416
Lord Okubo!

07:12.333 --> 07:15.125
Lord Okubo, please.

07:15.208 --> 07:18.083
If we don't exterminate
the shizoku in this war,

07:18.166 --> 07:21.250
they're sure to revolt
against the new age!

07:21.333 --> 07:24.833
Please grant the police officers
permission to carry guns.

07:26.458 --> 07:28.458
-I will not.
-Why?

07:28.958 --> 07:33.125
How are we supposed to protect you
from a potential assassination attempt?

07:33.208 --> 07:34.958
Take their swords away.

07:36.375 --> 07:38.666
-I will allow no more than that.
-Mr. Okubo!

07:40.291 --> 07:44.666
Heavy-handed oppression
will only result in more uprisings.

07:44.750 --> 07:47.625
Recall what happened in Kyoto
at the end of the Edo period.

07:47.708 --> 07:52.833
How many of our comrades fell
to the shizoku's swords!

07:53.875 --> 07:59.375
If highly skilled samurai were to plot
our assassination, we couldn't stop them!

07:59.458 --> 08:03.666
We need guns to protect Japan
in the coming era!

08:04.416 --> 08:07.291
What good does it do
to use force against force?!

08:08.500 --> 08:14.041
What do you think Japan needs
in order to grow strong as a nation?

08:14.125 --> 08:17.041
-The people!
-It's the people I want to protect!

08:17.125 --> 08:21.291
You cannot win public support by force!
Do you not understand that?!

08:25.708 --> 08:26.791
Kawaji.

08:28.583 --> 08:30.708
The shizoku will no longer be needed.

08:31.208 --> 08:32.166
However,

08:33.250 --> 08:36.583
unless we find a way to coexist…

08:40.083 --> 08:42.166
this country has no future.

09:05.083 --> 09:08.833
I… will not give up.

09:58.791 --> 10:05.791
THE KODOKU PROJECT

10:10.541 --> 10:11.750
Mr. Kawaji.

10:15.250 --> 10:16.250
Come in.

10:19.375 --> 10:20.708
Excuse me, sir.

10:23.833 --> 10:26.666
A telegram from Okubo for you.

10:29.083 --> 10:30.750
To Toshiyoshi Kawaji.

10:31.250 --> 10:35.750
We must discuss the future of the police.

10:36.250 --> 10:38.250
I await you in Tokyo.

11:24.666 --> 11:26.875
-Futaba.
-Yes?

11:27.458 --> 11:28.458
Go join them.

11:30.416 --> 11:32.833
-Is that all right?
-Yeah.

11:36.291 --> 11:37.750
Thank you.

11:41.958 --> 11:42.875
You sure?

11:43.958 --> 11:46.125
We have two days until the rendezvous.

11:46.208 --> 11:47.208
And besides,

11:48.125 --> 11:50.583
these could be our last days together.

12:10.083 --> 12:12.250
So that's how you look now.

12:14.000 --> 12:15.208
How I look now?

12:18.333 --> 12:21.583
Like a father watching his child.

12:30.666 --> 12:33.041
Did having a family make you happy?

12:37.208 --> 12:38.041
It did.

12:45.708 --> 12:47.875
What's it like having a real family?

13:20.000 --> 13:23.208
I'd sacrifice everything to protect them.

13:25.208 --> 13:28.416
It taught me a way of life
aside from killing.

13:38.333 --> 13:39.583
As for me…

13:42.500 --> 13:44.833
if I knew every day would be like this…

13:47.000 --> 13:49.750
I'd have been better off dying
in the succession match.

13:50.250 --> 13:51.708
I've thought that many times.

13:53.250 --> 13:54.250
Iroha.

13:54.791 --> 13:56.250
You've got it wrong. I--

13:56.333 --> 13:57.416
I know.

14:01.208 --> 14:02.375
I know.

14:07.416 --> 14:08.750
I'm going for a walk.

14:20.416 --> 14:22.833
What do you mean,
if our siblings were in trouble?

14:22.916 --> 14:24.416
Tell us the details.

14:24.500 --> 14:29.625
Shujiro Saga and Iroha Kinugasa are bound
to get killed unless you do something.

14:31.875 --> 14:33.083
You don't mean…

14:33.750 --> 14:34.750
Gentosai?

14:34.833 --> 14:37.625
Hey! Well done. You nailed it.

14:37.708 --> 14:40.583
There's a festival on
at the shrine up ahead.

14:40.666 --> 14:42.541
That's where the two of them are.

14:43.041 --> 14:45.000
As well as Gentosai.

14:45.833 --> 14:46.916
You…

14:47.791 --> 14:48.708
Who are you?

14:49.291 --> 14:50.708
Good question.

14:51.333 --> 14:53.958
Lately, I'm not sure
even I know the answer.

14:56.375 --> 14:57.750
Better hurry.

15:05.958 --> 15:07.083
Kyojin.

15:07.875 --> 15:10.375
What was that about? Who's Gentosai?

15:10.458 --> 15:14.833
Shinnosuke, there are some things
you're better off not knowing.

15:14.916 --> 15:16.000
But--

15:18.708 --> 15:24.375
Since we're in it, we might as well enjoy
this game they call the Kodoku.

16:12.750 --> 16:19.166
The eighth of the Kyohachi-ryu successors,
Iroha Kinugasa.

16:20.250 --> 16:22.291
I found you.

16:25.541 --> 16:26.583
It can't be…

16:48.875 --> 16:50.708
All right. Let's get started.

16:50.791 --> 16:52.000
Right!

16:53.083 --> 16:53.958
Here we go!

17:50.666 --> 17:52.416
Found you.

17:55.833 --> 17:56.916
Kokushu!

18:04.000 --> 18:06.458
It's about time we settled this!

18:10.666 --> 18:13.166
Get back!

18:25.875 --> 18:27.541
I knew it.

18:28.208 --> 18:30.958
Nothing beats fighting you to the death.

18:31.708 --> 18:33.916
You only kill for the thrill of it.

18:34.000 --> 18:35.958
Look who's talking.

18:37.083 --> 18:38.583
It's pathetic.

18:39.333 --> 18:41.375
Everything is so pathetic!

18:43.916 --> 18:46.833
And I'll destroy it all!

18:47.333 --> 18:48.666
Stop it!

18:55.250 --> 18:56.708
What's that, little miss?

18:58.458 --> 19:01.041
Why do you kill innocent people?

19:02.375 --> 19:03.458
You're no samurai!

19:03.541 --> 19:04.833
Futaba! Stay back!

19:07.083 --> 19:08.625
Then what is a samurai?

19:14.125 --> 19:15.291
Answer me that,

19:16.166 --> 19:17.166
little miss.

19:18.916 --> 19:20.916
Don't, Bukotsu. Let her go.

19:22.541 --> 19:24.416
If I killed this girl,

19:25.875 --> 19:27.833
I reckon you'd fight me then.

19:27.916 --> 19:29.583
No. Don't do it.

19:30.083 --> 19:31.125
Don't do it!

21:00.500 --> 21:02.083
Move it!

21:03.583 --> 21:04.583
Take that!

21:16.750 --> 21:18.333
Move! Out of the way!

21:36.083 --> 21:38.875
You have no chance with that arm.
Just give up.

21:40.750 --> 21:42.791
You're telling me to give up?

21:44.791 --> 21:47.333
It's 'cause we gave up
that we ended up this way.

21:49.875 --> 21:51.916
How did it feel to have your sword taken?

21:54.083 --> 21:56.333
Have you been happy?

22:00.250 --> 22:01.250
I've been happy.

22:01.333 --> 22:03.375
Then why are you here?

22:04.625 --> 22:09.791
In the end, the only way you can
prove it to yourself is to kill people.

22:12.333 --> 22:15.458
You can't even save
a single person without killing, can you?

22:21.208 --> 22:23.541
The era of the samurai is over?

22:24.416 --> 22:26.541
I don't give a damn.

22:27.041 --> 22:28.000
All we have to do

22:28.958 --> 22:31.166
is build it all over again!

22:40.333 --> 22:41.541
Move!

23:47.458 --> 23:49.333
I found you.

24:14.208 --> 24:15.791
Kokushu!

24:21.083 --> 24:22.500
Enough of this!

24:25.041 --> 24:26.416
Take that!

24:28.541 --> 24:29.583
Run!

25:14.875 --> 25:16.708
That was a good move.

25:19.458 --> 25:21.541
But you're done for.

25:22.250 --> 25:24.541
Any last words?

25:27.333 --> 25:29.041
If that's all you've got…

25:31.125 --> 25:33.625
you won't be able to defeat my brothers.

25:35.458 --> 25:36.875
You can rest assured.

25:37.958 --> 25:41.458
Everything shall soon perish.

26:11.250 --> 26:15.333
The fourth of the Kyohachi-ryu successors,

26:16.041 --> 26:18.125
Shikura Adashino.

26:37.416 --> 26:39.208
I can't believe he dodged that too.

26:41.250 --> 26:43.500
And now the third,

26:45.500 --> 26:48.000
Sansuke Gion.

27:24.666 --> 27:26.166
You monster!

27:42.333 --> 27:43.375
Sansuke.

27:44.833 --> 27:45.875
In time with me.

27:45.958 --> 27:47.000
Got it.

28:00.041 --> 28:02.000
He's way too strong.

28:04.000 --> 28:05.083
Run!

28:13.083 --> 28:15.166
Iroha! Let's move!

29:03.000 --> 29:04.958
Move!

29:05.666 --> 29:06.500
Move!

33:45.166 --> 33:47.416
Kokushu the Manslayer…

33:56.000 --> 33:57.500
I am…

34:00.333 --> 34:02.708
happy.

34:24.708 --> 34:25.833
Shujiro!

34:26.958 --> 34:29.708
Shujiro!

35:22.708 --> 35:24.916
The first participant
to reach Chiryu-juku was…

35:27.458 --> 35:30.083
number 277, Kamuykocha.

35:31.791 --> 35:34.500
Yes! Splendid!

35:34.583 --> 35:36.750
His long trip from Ezo was worth it.

35:37.333 --> 35:40.916
And number 66, Bukotsu Kanjiya,
has been eliminated.

35:41.000 --> 35:44.083
-What did you say?
-Killed by number 108, Shujiro Saga.

35:44.166 --> 35:46.833
Well, well.
That's Kokushu the Manslayer for you.

35:46.916 --> 35:49.666
It's a shame to lose
Bukotsu the Savage Slasher.

35:51.375 --> 35:54.583
It only means that
yet another specter has vanished.

35:56.375 --> 35:59.458
For us, it's something to celebrate.

36:00.708 --> 36:01.666
I agree.

36:01.750 --> 36:02.708
Of course.

36:03.375 --> 36:06.333
Organizer. It's almost time.

36:11.625 --> 36:16.333
I have duties to attend to,
so I shall be taking my leave for now.

36:16.833 --> 36:19.208
Of course.
The Superintendent General is a busy man.

36:19.291 --> 36:20.333
So,

36:21.208 --> 36:22.291
the time has come.

36:24.500 --> 36:28.458
I hope you continue to enjoy
the Kodoku, gentlemen.

36:49.083 --> 36:51.916
I've already telegrammed them
the meeting place.

36:52.708 --> 36:55.750
Good. Keep the rich bastards entertained.

36:55.833 --> 36:57.208
Understood, sir.

37:12.416 --> 37:13.291
Come in.

37:14.666 --> 37:15.791
Excuse me, sir.

37:18.375 --> 37:21.625
It seems Kawaji returned from
his business trip a little while ago.

37:22.875 --> 37:25.541
I'll go see him right away.
Get the carriage ready.

37:25.625 --> 37:26.625
Yes, sir.

37:26.708 --> 37:28.958
You still can't get hold of Shinpei?

37:30.125 --> 37:33.625
No, sir. I sent someone to his home,
but he didn't seem to be back yet.

37:33.708 --> 37:36.041
Should we ask the police
to conduct a search?

37:38.166 --> 37:42.750
No. Have the Home Ministry staff members
split up and try to find him.

37:43.250 --> 37:44.250
Yes, sir.

38:36.541 --> 38:37.750
What are you--

38:50.125 --> 38:53.000
It's been a long time, Lord Okubo.

38:55.416 --> 38:59.833
Hanjiro! You're… alive?

39:00.666 --> 39:02.333
I'm sorry to disappoint you,

39:02.416 --> 39:05.000
but Kawaji is not headed this way.

39:08.583 --> 39:09.666
What do you mean?

39:09.750 --> 39:13.708
I have a message from him instead.

39:14.916 --> 39:16.125
"Farewell."

40:09.791 --> 40:10.916
What is…?

40:12.791 --> 40:15.166
Just what is going on?

40:18.458 --> 40:21.583
OKAZAKI-JUKU

40:25.000 --> 40:28.333
Where do you think Iroha went off to?

40:28.875 --> 40:30.916
Knowing her, she'll be just fine.

40:32.291 --> 40:34.583
Extra!

40:34.666 --> 40:37.166
Extra!

40:37.666 --> 40:38.833
Extra!

40:41.125 --> 40:43.166
Extra!

40:44.583 --> 40:46.500
Shujiro, this is…

40:47.791 --> 40:49.458
Lord Okubo was killed?

40:51.583 --> 40:53.375
But why?

40:56.333 --> 40:58.000
This is no coincidence.

40:59.458 --> 41:00.541
What?

41:02.041 --> 41:03.833
The Kodoku's involved with this.

41:07.125 --> 41:08.541
Are you Mr. Saga?

41:10.541 --> 41:11.625
Who's asking?

41:11.708 --> 41:13.250
A message from Mr. Maejima.

41:13.333 --> 41:16.625
"I am returning to Tokyo for an emergency.
Keep heading for Tokyo."

41:16.708 --> 41:18.083
That's all.

41:20.708 --> 41:21.791
Understood.

41:22.291 --> 41:23.500
Goodbye, then.

41:27.625 --> 41:28.458
Futaba.

41:30.958 --> 41:33.083
We'll get to Tokyo as fast as we can.

41:35.416 --> 41:36.500
All right.

41:43.708 --> 41:45.750
Look out! A carriage is coming!

42:35.041 --> 42:37.458
Don't move too much.
It'll open up the wound.

42:38.791 --> 42:39.875
Thanks.

42:51.208 --> 42:52.791
Hey, you two.

42:56.375 --> 42:57.750
I just had a dream.

43:00.541 --> 43:03.000
About when we all lived together.

43:05.333 --> 43:09.250
Sansuke and I were bickering
like we always did.

43:11.875 --> 43:13.541
Shikura-nii was strong.

43:15.333 --> 43:17.750
We all used to smile back then.

43:20.583 --> 43:21.625
Yeah.

43:22.625 --> 43:24.041
We sure did.

43:26.291 --> 43:28.875
If we had the succession match back then…

43:31.250 --> 43:32.958
I'd be dead.

43:39.458 --> 43:41.708
It's thanks to Shu-nii running away…

43:47.083 --> 43:49.166
that I'm still alive now.

43:56.208 --> 43:58.708
But until we defeat Gentosai…

44:01.250 --> 44:03.416
we can't move forward.

44:16.541 --> 44:18.291
We'll take him down,

44:19.833 --> 44:21.583
all of us siblings together.

44:24.291 --> 44:25.375
That bastard…

44:27.958 --> 44:30.333
We can't beat him
unless we're all together.

44:36.666 --> 44:37.750
You're right.

44:39.416 --> 44:40.708
We just gotta do it.

44:41.750 --> 44:42.583
Yeah.

44:43.416 --> 44:46.041
Let's start by getting
all the siblings together.

45:03.000 --> 45:04.541
At Shimizudani in Kioi-cho…

45:05.041 --> 45:06.291
He actually did it!

45:06.375 --> 45:08.833
Organizer is truly a formidable man.

45:08.916 --> 45:11.833
This will allow us to focus on the Kodoku.

45:11.916 --> 45:12.875
Indeed.

45:13.458 --> 45:16.291
We still have
many remarkable participants left.

45:16.791 --> 45:18.708
The weak ones are gone.

45:18.791 --> 45:21.416
Only the strong remain now.

45:32.208 --> 45:34.458
CHIRYU, OKAZAKI, HAMAMATSU, SHIMADA

45:37.125 --> 45:38.333
Well, gentlemen.

45:38.833 --> 45:41.750
I hope you continue to enjoy the Kodoku.

45:43.166 --> 45:44.583
Cheers.

45:44.666 --> 45:45.708
-Wait for me.
-Run!

45:46.291 --> 45:47.291
He's right behind us!

45:51.000 --> 45:52.625
Let's play some more.

45:57.250 --> 45:58.791
Well, lucky me.

45:59.291 --> 46:01.125
I was short on tags.

46:09.791 --> 46:10.791
Good.

46:10.875 --> 46:12.333
That should be enough.

46:14.375 --> 46:17.000
You wanna fight too, sir?

46:19.375 --> 46:20.375
Come on, why not?

46:20.458 --> 46:21.958
It's fun.

46:49.250 --> 46:51.625
Really? You couldn't kill them?

46:52.125 --> 46:53.958
I even gave you their location.

47:08.833 --> 47:12.250
Keep killing each other
until only one is left standing.

47:37.750 --> 47:40.666
LAST SAMURAI STANDING

47:40.750 --> 47:43.416
END OF CHAPTER ONE

51:28.125 --> 51:31.625
Subtitle translation by: Lewis Williams
